first('2. Definitions\n\n3. Architecture',
     '2. Definitions\nAudio Visual Encoding (AVE): A proposed schema for presenting selected system information through a user interface; no neural interface or direct control of perception is established.\nConsumer: A software component that requests display or relay of a defined payload.\nOperator: The intended human recipient or sender in the model; identity and interface delivery do not establish current consent or understanding.\nAVE Signal: A typed, bounded message with source, payload, timestamp, and policy metadata.\nSignal Class: A draft category for payload complexity; it is not a measured bandwidth, safety, or perceptual-capacity guarantee.\n\n3. Architecture', 'AVE definitions')
